The meshes in this folder are built from NASA's OpenVSP model of its six-seat Quadrotor concept, collective-control
version (file quadcollflap.vsp3, sha256 a2b582d8b0e5ecdda9314f6e6fd36837fc975837919d64a88a6252dc58346ce4, in
quadrotor-vsp.zip, linked from https://www.nasa.gov/reference/uam-refs/). The model is one of NASA's reference
vehicles for Urban Air Mobility; under the NASA media usage guidelines (nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media)
NASA's 3D model files "generally are not subject to copyright in the United States". NASA is acknowledged here and
does not endorse PteroSim. No NASA insignia, logotype or identifier appears on the meshes or their textures.

Changes made here: the geometry was tessellated with OpenVSP 3.56 and split by component. PteroLabs rebuilt the
airframe as one closed hull with blended joints, cut the doors and the windscreen as real openings, modelled the
detail the concept model leaves out (door grooves and levers, grab bars, boarding steps, roof slots and side
louvres, panel seams and fasteners, a pitot, an antenna, blade cuffs), unwrapped the result, and painted and baked
its own textures in four liveries: taxi, rescue, liner and police. The police livery carries the word "POLICE" and
no real force's insignia.

Each livery folder holds body.glb, the airframe, in the flight model's frame (X aft, Y right, Z up, origin at the
VSP file's Center-Of-Mass marker), and rotor_1.glb to rotor_4.glb, each rotor about its own hub and numbered as in
Propulsion.xml; metres.
